Add GitHub Actions secret scanner workflow (Task #741)

Original task: extend the existing fast secret scanner
(scripts/secret-scan.sh, added in Task #732, currently only run via
scripts/post-merge.sh after Replit merges) to also run as a GitHub
Actions check on every pull request and on pushes to main, so leaks
are caught before reaching the main branch.

Changes:
- New workflow .github/workflows/secret-scan.yml
  - Triggers: pull_request, push to main, workflow_dispatch
  - Single job on ubuntu-latest that checks out the repo
    (fetch-depth: 0 so git ls-files in the scanner sees the full
    tracked file set) and runs `bash scripts/secret-scan.sh`
  - The scanner exits 1 on any match, which fails the job and
    produces a red required check on the PR.
- New SECURITY.md at repo root documenting:
  - What the scanner detects
  - Where it runs (post-merge locally + GitHub Actions on PRs/main)
  - What contributors should do on a failure (remove + rotate, or
    narrow the pattern / add a SKIP_REGEX exclusion)
  - How to run it locally

Verification:
- Ran `bash scripts/secret-scan.sh` locally — clean
  (5465 files scanned, no findings) with the new files in place.

No deviations from the task spec.

